WEBVTT

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:20.250
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:20.250
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:20.250
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:05.750
Dreams of the Morning, Songs of the Night

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:05.750
Chapter 1

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:09.150
How did it go ?

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.150
I tried so
hard this time...

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.150
I hope my ranking went up.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.200
First place,
Moritz von Haase.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.710
Second place,
Johann Gottholp von Bertz.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:35.140
Third place,
Erich von Warburg.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:38.150
I guess there's no change in
the top three reserved seats.

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.660
Reserved seats, huh ?

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.560
I guess I'm stuck in
third place until graduation.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.020
Won't your parents
be happy about that ?

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:47.480
My parents died in the war,
but my grandfather will...

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.330
It's nice that he
expects more of me, but...

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.890
How about you, Karl ?

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:55.170
I was 36th.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.170
I went down 8.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:00.020
I guess those
are free seats.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.140
I want a reserved seat.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:03.270
I would be fine
with 3rd place.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:06.900
Moritz !

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.360
I won't go for first place, so you
don't need to worry about me !

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.700
He's not friendly, is he ?

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.460
No, he prefers
to be a loner.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.650
He isn't a bad person, though.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:25.410
By the way, is there any
good way to boost my grades ?

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.800
Well, you model students ?

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.450
If there is,
I'd like to know.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.950
We'll be graduating this year.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:36.250
I want to be first in our class
just once before we graduate.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:39.710
I guess there are headaches
for the top students as well.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.110
Speaking of first
in their class...

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.940
...do you remember the guy who was first in
the class that graduated two years ago ?

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.330
Two years ago ?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.090
You mean Reinhard von Musel  ?

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.350
That's right, him.

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.020
He also preferred to be alone.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:56.860
He was unapproachable
because he was too great.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:58.530
He was different from Haase.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.400
Besides, he had
Kircheis with him.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:02.950
Yeah.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.270
He was a good senpai.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:07.540
He was always gentle
and kind to lower classmen.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:13.430
But I heard that those two beat
up 20 upperclassmen one time.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.580
I never heard about that.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.140
Anyway, what's that got
to do with anything ?

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:21.450
I heard they're
coming here today.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.150
Really ?
But why ?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.170
I don't know.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.450
But he was promoted
to captain recently.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.630
He's become a captain
at the age of 17.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:32.150
He's really something.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:35.020
He is the younger brother
of Countess Grunewald.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.110
Of course he's special.

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.900
No, it's not that.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.300
He has already had
some military achievements.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.510
I've heard
about that, too.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:46.110
He annihilated an enemy
front line base in his first battle...

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:49.010
...and he sank an enemy
cruiser with a destroyer.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.870
That's great for a
first in his class.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.000
First in his class, huh ?

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:26.800
Captain Reinhard von Musel
and Lieutenant Siegfried Kircheis.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:29.130
That's very impressive.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.200
Especially Musel, you
were first in your class...

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:35.320
...and you have become a
captain in just two years.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.570
That's a record for our school.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:42.760
It makes me, who was vice principal
when you were a student here, proud.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.020
Thank you.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.640
I also want to congratulate you
on your advancement, Admiral Steger.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:52.450
No, I was advanced to principal
just because I will retire soon.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.790
Anyway, what has brought
you here this time ?

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.660
I have been promoted, but until I receive
our next assignment, we have no job.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.070
It's part of our duty to observe
a military preparatory school.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:02.850
I see.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:05.800
You're welcome to stay here.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.570
I want you to tell the
students stories of the war.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:10.760
I will.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:15.270
In the 9th year of the Imperial Century,
the great Kaiser Rudolf...

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:25.560
...invented a way to eliminate weak genes and created policies to eliminate the weak from society.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:28.720
Mankind is always supported
and advanced by the elite...

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.370
...and a society that supports the weak leads to the deterioration of mankind.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:41.240
The great Kaiser especially focused on genetics in order to bring a bright future to mankind.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.300
People with genetic abnormalities
were forcibly sterilized...

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:50.800
...and people are now becoming free
of genetic diseases and abnormalities.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:56.250
Also, potential and willingness to work
have been found to be passed on by genes.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.760
Because of this, today's
policies have been formed:

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:04.980
People with strong genes were given noble status and people with weak genes became slaves.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:07.930
This is ridiculous.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:11.880
Lord Reinhard.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:12.950
Please wait a moment.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.820
It's fine.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:29.300
There's no surveillance.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.390
I can't believe I put up with
that class for five years.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.050
I'm amazed
by my perseverance.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:43.370
You were holding back, then ?

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.430
Genes decide everything ?

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:51.840
How ridiculous.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:55.950
Individuals are not
responsible for their genes.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.730
Individuals are individuals.

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:01.030
Family lines or genetics have nothing
to do with the abilities of the individual.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:02.870
People who believe that
genes decide everything...

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:07.390
...are truly worthless people who
can only do what they are told.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:13.540
People who boast of their ancestry have nothing that they can boast about in themselves.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:15.810
Those people are the ones
that I truly disrespect.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:19.550
It's true that Lord
Reinhard and Lady Annerose...

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:22.800
...have genes passed
down from Mr. Sebastian.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:27.900
It's been a while since we visited our
alma mater, but there was nothing to gain.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:32.780
I've realized the
need for reformation.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:36.290
But the students respect you.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:40.900
We gained enough just from
knowing that there are people...

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:45.150
...who don't look down on people
just because of their family lines.{ we gained that }

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:46.150
For our future.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:09:01.540
There are new orders for Captain Reinhard
von Musel and Lieutenant Siegfried Kircheis.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:05.230
Please report to the Military
Assignment Office tomorrow.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:08.070
Where is our next assignment ?

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:11.390
You are to report to the
Regional Military Police Office.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.240
Military Police ?

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.660
I will be waiting
for you tomorrow.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.500
Military Police ?

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:21.860
Us ?

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.550
What kind of joke is this ?
Are they trying to be funny ?

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:29.720
There's no need
to get angry.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:34.940
It's a job where we take away the
weak's right to affirm or deny !

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:37.690
They're going to make
me do such things ?

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:43.010
It might be a good opportunity to learn
the inner workings of the military police.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:46.600
That is one of the places that
needs to be reformed the most.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:55.900
You always take everything
in a positive light.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:10:01.650
I am satisfied as long as I am assigned
to the same post as Lord Reinhard.

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.980
Lord Reinhard takes
this for granted...

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:11.510
...but we could be assigned to
different posts when we're reassigned.

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:15.890
If there is no one between Lord
Reinhard and his surroundings...

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:19.100
...there will be
some kind of clash.

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:34.050
Is this seat taken ?

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:35.150
No.

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:40.170
As always, the
cafeteria food is meager.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.560
It's not like they don't
have a budget for this.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:47.640
People working at the cafeteria are
selling school supplies on the black market...

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:48.220
What ?

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:49.530
That's the rumor.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:50.740
Really ?

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:53.080
It's a rumor.
I don't know if it's true.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.690
Hey, Karl !

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:48.500
Karl !

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:49.550
Karl !

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:03.950
Hey, Karl !

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:10.810
Reifeisen is really
a trouble maker.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:14.500
What is he thinking, sneaking out of
the dorm in the middle of the night ?

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.690
It's probably useless to look
for him on the school grounds.

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:19.430
He must have gone out for some
fun and failed to come back in time.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:24.550
He wouldn't do such a stupid
thing and lower his grades.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.100
He's concerned about his grades.

00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:30.950
At any rate, he really
is a troublemaker.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:31.740
Hey.

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:33.050
Let's look over there.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.430
He's dead.

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:04.900
Why is there such disorder in this prestigious military school ?

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:06.080
Clear a path !

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:09.800
Principal Steger.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:10.700
Please.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.270
What's going on ?

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:25.680
5th year student,
Karl von Reifeisen.

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:28.170
We initiated a
campus-wide search for him...

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:30.500
...when we discovered he was missing
from his dormitory this morning.

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:35.320
These students found
him lying here, just like this.

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:39.350
Was it an accident ?

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:41.930
This storage is
locked from outside.

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:44.260
We haven't touched anything yet...

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:48.340
...but there is nothing that
could have hurt him like that.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:50.720
In other words, it's murder ?

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:55.890
And the fact that the weapon is
gone is proof that this is murder ?

00:13:56.860 --> 00:13:59.070
That's the only
conclusion I can come to.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.460
What should we do, Principal ?

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:06.550
We must report it to the military police
even if we don't tell the normal police.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:09.610
Are you saying that we should
announce this accident publicly ?

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:10.950
No, sir.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:17.110
At any rate, send
the students away.

00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:22.560
Preserve the crime scene
and summon the instructors !

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:37.890
What is it, Lord Reinhard ?

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:41.960
Kircheis, there was
an interesting incident.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:46.930
No, the incident itself wasn't, but the
reaction of the MPs was interesting.

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:48.600
What kind of
incident was it ?

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:54.810
An elderly female civilian had
three sons drafted and lost all three.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:59.620
So she stomped on the portrait of
Kaisers Rudolf and Friedrich IV.

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:07.550
It's you Kaisers' fault
that I lost three sons !

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:11.220
I have no other way to
show my gratitude to you !

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:20.260
The neighbor reported this,
and the woman was arrested.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:28.020
The rebellious Alliance is the one to
be blamed, but she blamed the Kaiser.

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:32.530
Her actions are
unpatriotic and uncivil.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:38.890
Those who do not work for the country do
not deserve to be treated like human beings.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:42.630
She must be punished.

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:47.240
In other words, she must
be tortured to death.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:49.100
That's the way the 
military police do things.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.310
Did you know this, Kircheis ?

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:56.680
The military police chief has
two sons in the military...

00:15:56.680 --> 00:16:01.300
...and he used his authority to put them
in positions in the rear where it's safe.

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:03.860
That, too, is the way
nobility does things.

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:05.810
That's right.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:10.020
But the person in charge of this incident did not follow the low ways of his superiors.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:19.700
He went to the neighbor who 
witnessed the incident and arrested him.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:26.450
He watched the
woman commit the crime...

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:29.350
...but he just watched her do
it and did not try to stop her.

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:31.700
This is not the
way of a true citizen.

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:36.810
He reported it later on, hoping to be rewarded
but that's just a way to cover up his own crime.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:39.770
It must be that he secretly agreed
with the woman in his heart...

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:43.090
...for he didn't stop her from
stepping on the Kaiser's portrait.

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:44.890
He is practically an accomplice.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:50.710
The woman cannot be punished
without punishing him.

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:54.700
On the other hand, the woman
was imprisoned and questioned...

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.200
...but was not
physically punished.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:03.350
She must be insane to step
on the portrait of the Kaiser.

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:06.350
It is pointless to
torture an insane person.

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:11.340
People who learned of this
incident secretly shouted for joy.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.030
Who was the
one in charge ?

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.610
Just as I thought, he
wasn't a regular MP officer.

00:17:20.610 --> 00:17:26.220
He is a fleet judge advocate who became
a military police officer for training purposes.

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:28.000
He was just like we are now.

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:30.070
His name is...

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.240
...Kesler.

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:34.240
Commander Ulrich Kesler.

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.100
He's a very
interesting person.

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:42.450
He makes me think, showing
that there are other ways...

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.070
I want to meet him.

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:46.020
I wonder if he's still
assigned to the MPs.

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:47.260
I'll check on it.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.210
He has already returned
to duty in the fleet.

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:59.030
Duty in a remote region.

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:03.410
I guess people with an uncompromising
mindset cannot go with the mainstream.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:04.770
Yes.

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:07.710
Ulrich Kesler.

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:09.000
I will remember him.

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:14.870
By the way, what
happened to the woman ?

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:18.170
This paper only reports
that she was exiled.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.960
I will look it up.

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:27.870
What happened ?

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:34.150
After she was exiled, she refused
to eat, and she died of malnutrition.

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:45.530
Minor opposition at the scene is
not the answer to the problem.

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:52.020
This society needs to be reformed completely
so that this nonsense will not happen.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.410
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:19:01.090
And we must do it ourselves,
and not wait for others to do it.

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:04.030
Yes, just as you
say, Lord Reinhard.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:10.150
Captain Reinhard von Musel and
Lieutenant Siegfried Kircheis.

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:12.590
The Chief of the Military
Police wants to see you.

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:13.530
Please come immediately.

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.050
Things happen as soon
as we speculate about it.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:21.400
What do you think has happened ?

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:23.500
Who knows ?

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:28.620
So that's the reason why the report
to the MPs was delayed 3 hours.

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:33.050
Reifeisen, the victim,
is from a well known family.

00:19:33.050 --> 00:19:37.900
And if it's an incident at a military school
where many noble children attend...

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:40.600
...the school must
treat it carefully.

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:41.800
It's understandable.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:48.550
Anyway, I will leave this
matter to you, Captain Musel.

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:51.570
I want you to check on
this with Lieutenant Kircheis.

00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:53.450
Us two ?

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:58.830
We are just observers
from the space fleet.

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.630
I know of your accomplishments
on the front lines.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:05.890
At the same time, I'm hoping
you also have some detective skills.

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:11.240
In addition, you visited that military
school just a couple of days ago.

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:14.270
You must know more
about the school than us.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:21.660
Also, when we talk to the students, things will go smoother if you do it, since you are similar in age.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:24.050
I will give you full
responsibility for a week.

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:28.100
But of course,
Captain Musel...

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:32.100
...it's not that there's no one
suitable for the situation in the MPs.

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:38.110
I can order others to do this if
things get beyond your ability.

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:40.430
I understand.

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:41.900
I will do my best.

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:48.130
Lord Reinhard.

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:51.350
There is no reason
to play their cheap game.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:55.530
It's a reluctant job
at a reluctant position...

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:58.660
...but I cannot back
down without doing it.

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:02.640
But there is no need for
you to be good at everything.

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:10.370
It is more important for you to be able to direct the masses and rule than to be a skillful detective.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:16.430
I know.

00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:19.060
They just want
to get rid of me.

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:22.380
I am the brother
of Countess Grunewald.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:27.550
If I die in their jurisdiction, they will be
charged for their mismanagement...

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:30.960
...so they want to get rid
of me as soon as I arrive.

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:33.330
I have been moved around because
of my accomplishments until now...

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:38.660
...but they could just move me if
I don't qualify for the position.

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:41.740
If you knew that, why ?

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.390
Say, Kircheis ?

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.790
We have never lost.

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:53.100
No matter to whom or how many.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.050
Right, Lord Reinhard.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.520
We will never lose.

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:01.020
Isn't that right ?

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:02.910
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:07.150
So I will not lose to
the enemy in front of us.

00:22:07.150 --> 00:22:08.810
No matter who.

00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:10.950
Even a sly criminal.

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:13.900
He doesn't know
how to back down.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:16.680
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:22:21.930 --> 00:22:25.110
It was Imperial Year 484.

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:28.850
Reinhard von Musel and
Siegfried Kircheis unexpectedly...

00:22:28.850 --> 00:22:35.100
...had to return to the military
school they had just visited.

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:41.260
Their visit's purpose is to investigate
the murder as military police.

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:42.400
To be continued

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:56.580
I don't wait to live a life of counting memories

00:22:44.650 --> 00:22:50.340
